## Does “the square kill the complex part”?

Not exactly. It doesn’t remove phase information — it removes the *complex phase of the total overlap*.

The magnitude squared still depends on the relative phases inside the sum.

Example:

If

$$
S = A_1 e^{i\phi_1} + A_2 e^{i\phi_2}
$$

then

$$
|S|^2
=====

A_1^2 + A_2^2

* 2 A_1 A_2 \cos(\phi_1 - \phi_2)
  $$

The cosine term carries interference.

So phase learning still happens.

